    "raw": "{\"ruleId\":\"item-f673fb67af1a\",\"class\":\"expressible\",\"constraints\":[{\"id\":\"domain-app-no-pg-import\",\"type\":\"forbiddenDependency\",\"severity\":\"high\",\"to\":\"package:pg\",\"scopePaths\":[\"src/domain/**\",\"src/app/**\"]},{\"id\":\"domain-no-pg-require\",\"type\":\"forbiddenPattern\",\"severity\":\"high\",\"pattern\":\"require\\\\(\\\\s*['\\\"]pg(/[^'\\\"]*)?['\\\"]\\\\s*\\\\)\",\"path\":\"src/domain/**\"},{\"id\":\"app-no-pg-require\",\"type\":\"forbiddenPattern\",\"severity\":\"high\",\"pattern\":\"require\\\\(\\\\s*['\\\"]pg(/[^'\\\"]*)?['\\\"]\\\\s*\\\\)\",\"path\":\"src/app/**\"}],\"coverage\":\"Any direct import edge from a src/domain or src/app module to the pg package: static import, import type, export-from and dynamic import(). It also catches require('pg') and TS import-equals require('pg') forms, including pg subpaths, in those directories.\",\"residual\":null,\"probes\":{\"violating\":[{\"patch\":\"--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/src/domain/db-probe.ts\\n@@ -0,0 +1,2 @@\\n+import { Pool } from 'pg';\\n+export const p = Pool;\\n\"},{\"patch\":\"--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/src/domain/req-probe.ts\\n@@ -0,0 +1,2 @@\\n+const pg = require('pg');\\n+export const q = pg;\\n\"},{\"patch\":\"--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/src/app/req-probe.ts\\n@@ -0,0 +1,2 @@\\n+import pg = require(\\\"pg\\\");\\n+export const r = pg;\\n\"}],\"compliant\":{\"patch\":\"--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/src/domain/clean-probe.ts\\n@@ -0,0 +1,1 @@\\n+export const clean = 1;\\n--- /dev/null\\n+++ b/src/infra/db/pg-probe.ts\\n@@ -0,0 +1,2 @@\\n+import { Pool } from 'pg';\\n+export const pool = Pool;\\n\"}},\"rationale\":\"The rule is a mechanical layering ban: the pg package must not be imported directly from files in two directories. The import-graph constraint scoped to src/domain/** and src/app/** catches ESM import edges. The line patterns add CommonJS and import-equals require('pg') forms. Imports of pg from infra stay allowed. No judgement of meaning or intent is needed.\"}",
